===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[work]] at a secondary job, often in the [[evening]] or during the [[night]].<ref name="Webster's c 2001"/> In American English, simply secondary employment,<ref>Mish, Drederick C. (ed.). 1995. ''Merriam-Webster's Collegiate Dictionary.'' 10th ed. Springfield, MA: Merriam-Webster.</ref> but in British English implying working secretly (i.e., not paying tax on the extra money earned).<ref>Treffry, Diana (ed.). 1999. ''Collins Paperback English Dictionary.'' 4th ed. Glasgow: HarperCollins.</ref>. By extension, to engage in an activity other than what one is known for, often in secret.

